      "body": "Why mark only the first and last rows? Every row in the range already gets `commented`.",
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "a1b2c3",
          "author": "Claude",
          "created": "2026-09-25T14:07:00.000Z",
          "body": "The bar is drawn per row, so the middle rows need `commented` to join up. `cm-start` and `cm-end` only tell the CSS where to inset and round the ends, so one range reads as one mark and two adjacent ranges stay visibly separate."
        }
      ]
